{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T14:12:29.975Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-27T14:12:29.975Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Review round 2 (short-prefix finding): the class rule is 'do not run a whole-input operation when the target lives in a bounded prefix' - the test-side face of the round-1 production rule. The budget test selected its fragment from the whole sixteen-megabyte document, paying paragraph()'s contract-mandated full-document uniqueness scan (measured 1295-2632ms across runs) for a passage that lives in a twelve-byte prefix. Fixed by selecting the fragment from the short prefix (identical bytes and offsets, so every assertion is unchanged) and budgeting the setup together with the bounded scans; the document build sits outside the timed region after one flake showed allocation cost does not belong in a budget. Package sweep for the class: every other large input in the suites is the assertion target itself (hostile budget cases, bundle size-refusal boundaries, digest fills), not unrelated setup; the production side of the rule was closed in round 1. Revert proof with the final form: reverting only the ancestry bound makes this test fail at 2395.5ms against its 100ms budget (24x over, deterministic); restored, 8/8 pass. Focused suites 36/36; lint, typecheck, docstring, duplication 0%, identity and dist checks all clean."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T14:12:29.975Z"}],"before_hash":"39e51db4945d7aeb4e9cddc6560bf937b172a8974d440bd492d31274eed6af8c","after_hash":"1da49c998885262f408e1d1eb9a10dc42ab95eb08dfb649be47766f93b39ad9b","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"821bd226ad4a42d031bb0d8c17b098057e0183068468e194dd0b2ac603fa2258"}
