{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T15:02:48.578Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T15:02:48.578Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"in_progress"}],"before_hash":"ae2e1edf8a9c43aae85150c0fc7243eadfb6fda3c7b3a7a7ad6b0007b775c133","after_hash":"a794944ad2e1543a08036a9168321f243b5735e342b81169850101e104676fd2","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7ce8fb0c4633f4df80f49bc1b17ae65c6adc446d50510b0dd8d846ba37dc398c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T15:12:31.784Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-27T15:12:31.783Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Review round 3: (1) BLOCKING, memory: the class rule is 'a consumer that reduces a sequence to a bounded working set must not first materialize the whole sequence'. The bound fix made sectionPath ask headingLines for every heading before the offset as one array, so a passage cited after four million headings in a supported 16 MB document exhausted a 256 MiB heap where the merge base's lazy matchAll iterator did not. headingLines is now a generator: sectionPath yields-and-reduces with O(1) memory (the round-1 offset bound intact), while paragraph() spreads it once because its uniqueness contract needs the full list exactly as the merge base did. Class sweep: hits() and the paragraph selection are contract-mandated whole-list operations (merge-base parity, not regressions); no other consumer materializes a reducible sequence. New guard: a heap-capped child probe (256 MiB, 4M headings before the passage) resolves the ancestry and exits 0 on the generator and FAILS on the reverted array version (child OOM, deterministic and load-independent) - revert proof run both ways. The harness's linear heading scan control now extracts and mutates the generator form (functionText gained a generator-signature probe) and still yields exactly one failure. (2) NON-BLOCKING, timing: the rule is 'suite timing budgets must tolerate concurrent-runner load'. The 8 MB whitespace case took 811 ms against its 400 ms limit under concurrent verification; the whitespace input is halved and every scan budget widened (whitespace 2000 ms, escaped 1000 ms, digit 800 ms, hostile heading production path 2500 ms) so a 10x loaded slowdown still passes while any super-linear regression still fails by orders of magnitude. These are load-tolerant smoke budgets, not constant-factor revert detectors - the tokenizer's linearity is structural (regex-free single pass) and the recorded old-vs-new measurement stands."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T15:12:31.784Z"}],"before_hash":"a794944ad2e1543a08036a9168321f243b5735e342b81169850101e104676fd2","after_hash":"81e1ba6c9d35d61868102b736e15ac9df515d1bbb850fdec84bff760308fb8cf","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"061c30095c4c9ee2fde85e0a1740ea69ece55f38cde6f463fb5ec941871712d0"}
